{
  "_doc": "Subscription plans and what their quotas are denominated in. This file exists because the dominant way our target users buy AI is a flat monthly plan, not metered API credit — so the honest headline number is not 'you spent $412', it is 'you paid $18 and consumed $412 of API-equivalent work, and you are 61% through this week's quota'. See docs/specs/Plan-And-Quota-Model.md.",
  "_contributing": "Plan prices and quota units change often and vary by region. Correcting one is a welcome PR — cite the vendor's pricing page.",
  "_verified_on": "2026-08-19",
  "_schema": 1,

  "_quota_doc": "quota.unit is what the vendor meters you in: 'credits' | 'prompts' | 'messages' | 'tokens' | 'none'. quota.windows lists each reset window the vendor enforces; a plan can have several at once (e.g. a 5-hour rolling cap AND a weekly cap). `amount: null` means the vendor publishes no number, so headroom is estimated from the user's own p90 instead of a published limit.",

