  "_currency_doc": "Indicative FX for the local-currency lens. These are display conversions, not accounting: a bill is settled in USD by most vendors, and the point of showing MYR/IDR/VND is that '$412/month' means something very different in Jakarta than in San Francisco. `daily_dev_rate_usd` is a coarse median local contract rate used only for the 'this month cost N days of your own billable time' framing — it is a conversation-starter, not a salary benchmark.",
